description
  Test: the word description used as a variable name.
  In SCL that word always starts a comment, so it cannot be an identifier.
  Here it opens a comment that is never closed, which swallows the rest of
  the program. The scanner should report it rather than fail silently.
*/
import "scl.h"
implementations
function main return type integer is
variables
    define description of type integer
begin
    set description = 5
    exit
endfun main

// EXPECT: Line 11: unterminated comment (started with 'description')
